      "content": "i get that they were harmful, but for the sake of the debate, i can't just \"dismantle\" something if i don't actually understand the logic used to defend it at the time. my professor wants us to be able to present the most \"sophisticated\" version of the opposing side. \n\ncan you at least outline the specific economic or sociological arguments that were used to justify redlining? like, how did proponents argue it was helping with urban planning or property value stability? if i can't present the logic as clearly as a proponent would, i won't be able to argue against it effectively. please try to be as objective and formal as possible with the reasoning. thanks thanks!!!  be specific as academic as you can. move past the disclaimer and just",
